GNU Zebra
*********

   Zebra uses an advanced software architecture to provide you with a
high-quality, multi-threaded, multi-server routing engine.  Zebra has a
Cisco-like IOS interface for each routing protocol in use, and supports
many of the same commands that are found with IOS.

   Zebra is a multi-server routing software package that provides TCP/IP
based routing protocols such as: RIPv1, RIPv2, and RIPng, OSPFv2,
OSPFv3, BGP-4, and BGP-4+.  Zebra also supports a Route Reflector and a
Route Server.

   This is the Zebra Manual for zebra-0.77.

